            "level": {
                "value": 4
            },
            "privateNotes": "",
            "publicNotes": "<p>A lone traveler strays into the woods and stumbles across a circle of mushrooms that tower overhead like trees, each one hollowed out and marked with holes. Numerous pairs of oversized, circular eyes suddenly glow from within the hollows. Within moments, a crowd of small, furry bipeds swarms the wanderer, each resembling a hybrid between a mouse and lizard. And then… the gerbies begin chattering in squeaky, high-pitched voices, bombarding the newcomer with greetings and questions. All welcoming, all smiling, all happy to meet a new friend!</p>\n<p>Gerbies live in quaint, communal societies where they craft all their material needs and practice vegetarianism. Knowing that not all places have the privilege of such harmony, gerbies make it their life's purpose to foster peace and friendship wherever they go. Gerbies value empathy and positive communication, and with their natural knack for both, they often appoint themselves as mediators for any conflicts in their vicinity. Conveniently, all it takes is a touch of magical persuasion—and in severe cases, memory modification—to resolve most disputes. Even without their mind-affecting powers, gerbies possess exceptionally pleasant smiles and exude disarming affability.</p>",
            "publication": {
                "license": "ORC",
                "remaster": true,
                "title": "Pathfinder Feybound"
            }
